{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[],"blocking":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `complete` to the `required` list of `pack_layer` in tracker_footprint.schema.json so the field is enforced, matching the ticket AC and the code that always emits it.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"block","evidence":["src/rebar/schemas/tracker_footprint.schema.json:145: \"required\": [\"logical_bytes\", \"file_count\", \"scope\"],","src/rebar/schemas/tracker_footprint.schema.json:150: \"complete\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }","src/rebar/_store/footprint.py:222-227 always returns a dict containing `complete`","Ticket AC: 'schema requires `complete` boolean to `pack_layer`' / 'schema requires pack.complete'"],"finding":"The tracker_footprint schema adds `complete` to pack_layer.properties but does not add it to the `required` list, so the schema does not enforce the field even though measure_tracker always emits it and the ticket AC states the schema should require pack.complete. A report omitting `complete` would validate as conformant, defeating the guarantee the code and tests rely on.","id":"0","impact":0.6,"location":"src/rebar/schemas/tracker_footprint.schema.json:145","norm_id":"nb3d089a13ca5790d","priority":0.6,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A future producer path that forgets to emit `complete` still passes schema validation, silently reintroducing the ambiguous whole-object-store reading the change set out to prevent."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Change the pack_layer `required` array to [\"logical_bytes\", \"file_count\", \"scope\", \"complete\"].","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_